"position":"1793815891642912001-78ef830e-64dc-4995-9892-5af5a5997690"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"9ebe6a931f16d42a78abd5d7be5f9a54603795c4d48fede46ec0e054b094761f","event_uuid":"c465bb09-ee96-4c53-a800-7a91a9ff5e49","position":{"commit_sha":"b797ddb3697c32761e14bb3d7be962d9f9616fdc","position":"1793825594956870001-c465bb09-ee96-4c53-a800-7a91a9ff5e49"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"d4fbde5bb895ec33c98fb8d45d29e2d71f34a4e06819750aa4d1fe7309a152d8","event_uuid":"ed856ea8-96c3-43f1-829b-59d6af67b326","position":{"commit_sha":"f1c0188175111a8e1b6dbec335751a7e044b97d1","position":"1793826711093676446-ed856ea8-96c3-43f1-829b-59d6af67b326"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"76b2497061ddfa8bc9f4330653fbec0af40be134cb8276884c32da6ac56ea01a","event_uuid":"012d5b84-9e9d-4077-aad4-9cd0b593ad06","position":{"commit_sha":"c27dc7ab5008fa6d38f455c248fa382cd9d582be","position":"1793828317047523001-012d5b84-9e9d-4077-aad4-9cd0b593ad06"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"1cf91f096c0dbe2665b51c590fc5701c8b566038ffb126d13a11a31561f8cda7","event_uuid":"39a0a1e7-47e9-4244-8cae-b3bd956bd09f","position":{"commit_sha":"ca980fb14818a5482ebd038919a5e1b1bc509cc2","position":"1793828338483286001-39a0a1e7-47e9-4244-8cae-b3bd956bd09f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"695714d3b09d9312db8afa0b36e7f180ceed6bc0495bdd4417149e6255d7edef","event_uuid":"77500a53-773b-4f53-afd5-0206c09285dd","position":{"commit_sha":"0d857c4fe14a601f094948228e35f666debe74ca","position":"1793828906545411001-77500a53-773b-4f53-afd5-0206c09285dd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Findings and verdicts (sandbox: 2 processes over one git store, each with its own `.rebar`, the blue-green view). Production check, read-only over SSM 2026-11-04: container rebar-mcp-1c8a67702f81-8093 started 08:58 PST, `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` absent, tracker at `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, process runs as root.\n\n- hlc.state / hlc.lock: no harm. With blue's cache 1 h ahead of the wall clock, blue wrote tkt-x at ahead+1. Green, with an empty cache, then ticked tkt-x at ahead+2: the witness floor (`_max_event_prefix`) comes from the shared tracker. Split caches gave equal ticks (both 1001 under a fixed clock) only when neither process had written in between, which means 2 concurrent events. `event_sort_key` orders those deterministically. Writers that see each other are serialized by `<tracker>/.ticket-write.lock`, which is shared. Left in place, with a comment in hlc.py.\n- recent-creates journal: harm. Blue recorded \"Fix the widget\". Blue's retry got a duplicate_warning; green's create of the same title got None. `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets = true` in rebar.toml. Moved to `<git dir>/rebar-recent-creates.{json,lock}`.\n- similar-ticket index (`.rebar/cache/similar-tickets`): a cache rebuilt from the shared tracker. Left in place, with a comment in index.py.\n- compact-worker.log: already sent to stderr in the MCP container by `compact.worker_log` (3300). No change.\n\nTests: the new tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py failed 3 of 4 on main (the HLC pin passed, as expected) and passes 4 of 4 after the change. 212 targeted tests pass, and 599 across the create, clock, store, similar and mechanism modules (the mechanism baseline drained `lock::recent-creates.lock`). make lint and make typecheck exit 0. make verify: 20779 passed, 2 failed in tests/interfaces/facades. Both of those fail on the unchanged base as well and are already tracked as bald-diagnostic-cricket and fibre-beamy-angora.","timestamp":1793825594956870001}],"created_at":1793798037827443001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f42703d1-feb3-409d-8dbc-b8f63328aab7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"eac3-3f1b-69bb-414e"},{"link_uuid":"ed856ea8-96c3-43f1-829b-59d6af67b326","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"09e8-294c-3024-4fa8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nIn the rebar-mcp container the tracker is `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets` (the shared `gerrit_mcp_tickets` volume), so `StorePaths(tracker).rebar_dir` (src/rebar/_store/paths.py `_rebar_dir`) is `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar`, on each container's writable layer (read-only SSM 2026-11-04: not mounted; absent in the container started 08:58 PST). `exemplary-silty-tuatara` moved the compaction lock and stamp into the tracker's git dir. The remaining tracker-sibling files are the HLC cache and lock (src/rebar/_store/hlc.py), the recent-creates journal and lock (src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py), the similar-ticket index (src/rebar/similar/index.py `index_dir`) and the compaction worker log (compact_trigger `_TRIGGER_LOG`, which the MCP container already sends to stderr via `compact.worker_log`).\n\n## Findings (sandbox: 2 processes, one git store, each with its own `.rebar`, as in tests/unit/test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars.py)\n- **`hlc.state`/`hlc.lock`: harmless.** `next_tick` returns `max(state, witness, physical_now)+1`, where the witness is the target ticket's largest committed event prefix (`_max_event_prefix`). A process with a fresh `.rebar` ticking a ticket after another wrote it at a value 1 hour ahead of the wall clock got exactly that value + 1, so per-ticket order never goes backwards. The store write lock is `<tracker>/.ticket-write.lock` (src/rebar/_store/lock.py `_acquire_once`), which is shared, and the transition and close paths tick under it after the earlier writer's file has landed (txn.py `prepare_transition_event_locked`, completion_txn.py). Split caches can produce an equal tick only for 2 events neither of which had seen the other (reproduced with a fixed clock: both 1001), and `event_sort_key` (src/rebar/reducer/_sort.py) orders equal prefixes deterministically by type and filename, the same as for 2 separate clones. The module docstring already declares the cache safe to lose.\n- **Recent-creates journal: harmful.** After one process records \"Fix the widget\", a second create with that title from the same `.rebar` gets the `duplicate_warning`; from a fresh `.rebar` it gets `None`. So every deploy drops the last 600 s of creates, and during the blue-green overlap a create on one container is invisible to the other. A create retried after a deploy drops its connection is exactly the duplicate this advisory exists to flag. `verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets = true` in rebar.toml, so the MCP server runs this probe. The ranked `similar_tickets` list still runs, but the `duplicate_warning` is lost.\n- **Similar-ticket index: harmless cache.** It is rebuilt from the shared tracker by catch-up; a loss costs one rebuild.\n\n## Approach\nFollow `exemplary-silty-tuatara`: keep the recent-creates journal and its lock in the tracker's git dir (`StorePaths(tracker).git_dir`, as `rebar-recent-creates.json` / `rebar-recent-creates.lock`), which is part of the store and shared by both containers and every worktree view. The journal's lock is already `sibling_exclusive_lock` (src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py), so only the location changes and no new primitive is added. The renamed lock gets a `# mechanism-ok: lock rebar-recent-creates.lock — <id>` marker. The old `.rebar/recent-creates.json` is ignored and left alone, since it only holds 600 s of state. For the HLC files and the similar index, leave the location and add a short comment stating why their loss is harmless.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py: journal and lock path moved to the git dir\n- src/rebar/_store/hlc.py: comment, no behaviour change\n- src/rebar/similar/index.py: comment, no behaviour change\n- tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py (new): 2-process regression\n- tests/unit/test_create_duplicate_warning.py: `_journal_path` helper follows the new location\n- .github/mechanism-baseline.json: drain the stale `lock::recent-creates.lock` entry with `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale`, as AGENTS.md requires when a change removes a mechanism\n\n## Testing\n- Failing first: the new test spawns 2 bounded children (through `_subprocess_env.subprocess_env`) over one git store, each rebinding `rebar._store.paths._rebar_dir` to its own dir; the first records a title and the second create with that title must get a `duplicate_warning`. It fails on current main.\n- Edge: a linked-worktree tracker (`.git` is a file) keeps the journal in its own git dir, and nothing is written under the sibling `.rebar`.\n- An HLC regression test: a process with a fresh `.rebar` ticking a ticket written at a value ahead of the wall clock returns a larger value (it pins the harmless verdict).\n- Existing suites: tests/unit/test_create_duplicate_warning.py, test_create_similar_tickets.py, tests/unit/test_hlc.py, tests/unit/store/ (store paths), test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars.py.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] [non-codebase] For each of `hlc.state`/`hlc.lock` and the recent-creates journal, the ticket records whether a per-container reset or split lock affects behaviour, with evidence; verified by the Findings section above and a closing comment.\n  provenance: environment=local macOS sandbox (2 processes over one git store, each with its own .rebar) plus the production rebar-mcp container listed read-only over SSM; principal=operator via the frontier AWS profile; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — the verdicts come from the sandbox runs recorded in Findings and the 2026-11-04 comment; the production step only listed /var/gerrit/site and changed nothing.\n- [x] The recent-creates journal and lock are store-scoped and shared by both MCP containers; verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py`, which fails on origin/main and passes after the change.\n- [x] The HLC verdict is pinned by a test in which a process with a fresh `.rebar` ticks a ticket above its committed prefix; verified by the same pytest run.\n- [x] Existing create, HLC and store tests still pass; verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_create_duplicate_warning.py tests/unit/test_create_similar_tickets.py tests/unit/test_hlc.py tests/unit/store tests/unit/test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars.py`.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0 (the mechanism gate exits 0 with the marker in place), and every src/rebar file stays at or under 800 lines.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py","reason":"keep the journal and lock in the tracker git dir"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"comment why the cache may be lost"},{"path":"src/rebar/similar/index.py","reason":"comment why the cache may be lost"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py","reason":"2-process regression test"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_create_duplicate_warning.py","reason":"journal path helper follows the move"},{"path":".github/mechanism-baseline.json","reason":"drain the stale recent-creates.lock entry"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","09e8-294c-3024-4fa8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d6eb947b-0b83-40cc-a871-e754acde8642","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1237-b65b-d7d2-4565","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP .rebar sidecars beyond compaction reset per deploy","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["17f7886d-7e79-48ab-a7e0-b8f9f8164b9e","bc77fab0-83fb-42b3-8bdd-1a9b3b6688e0","ad8c8514-c76b-447d-80a7-1c058352a68a","359320fa-8289-46bf-a178-d2cf5d909aaa","d6eb947b-0b83-40cc-a871-e754acde8642","78ef830e-64dc-4995-9892-5af5a5997690","c465bb09-ee96-4c53-a800-7a91a9ff5e49","ed856ea8-96c3-43f1-829b-59d6af67b326","012d5b84-9e9d-4077-aad4-9cd0b593ad06","39a0a1e7-47e9-4244-8cae-b3bd956bd09f","77500a53-773b-4f53-afd5-0206c09285dd"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793828906545411002,"uuid":"12023654-62fc-4da4-95d3-b3863445ff47"}